# GitHub CODEOWNERS
#
# Owners listed here are automatically requested for review on PRs that touch
# the matching paths. When combined with a branch-protection rule that
# requires "Require review from Code Owners", this enforces approval gates
# that cannot be self-approved by the PR author.
#
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern>  <owner1> <owner2> ...
# Last matching rule wins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security-sensitive files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The container CVE suppression file silently weakens the deploy-time CVE
# gate. Per docs/SECURITY_CVE_TRIAGE.md §7, any change MUST be approved by
# Security on-call — a self-approved suppression is a HIPAA-relevant finding.
# Enforced here (not just by convention) so a regular PR author cannot merge
# their own suppression entry.
/.trivyignore.yaml  @tabula-medica/security
